{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E9sdmYnbNJ35HxcJEGKaLj","type":"tool_result","content":"import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\n/// Thin wrapper around PostHog so the key and host live in one place.\nclass Analytics {\n  static Future<void> init() async {\n    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n    await Posthog().setup(config);\n  }\n\n  /// Sends one event. [props] is optional.\n  static Future<void> capture(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass Offer {\n  const Offer(this.bank, this.months, this.rate);\n  final String bank;\n  final int months;\n  final double rate;\n}\n\nconst _offers = [\n  Offer('Norbank', 12, 9.9),\n  Offer('Norbank', 24, 10.4),\n  Offer('Fjordcredit', 12, 8.7),\n  Offer('Fjordcredit', 36, 11.2),\n  Offer('Vestkapital', 24, 9.5),\n  Offer('Vestkapital', 48, 12.0),\n  Offer('Sparbank', 12, 10.9),\n  Offer('Sparbank', 60, 12.8),\n  Offer('Nordlån', 36, 10.1),\n  Offer('Nordlån', 60, 12.3),\n];\n\nclass OfferScreen extends StatelessWidget {\n  const OfferScreen({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Offers')),\n      body: ListView.builder(\n        itemCount: _offers.length,\n        itemBuilder: (context, i) {\n          final o = _offers[i];\n          return ListTile(\n            leading: const Icon(Icons.account_balance),\n            title: Text('${o.bank}, ${o.months} months'),\n            subtitle: Text('${o.rate.toStringAsFixed(1)}% APR'),\n            trailing: const Icon(Icons.chevron_right),\n            onTap: () {},\n          );\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass RegistrationScreen extends StatefulWidget {\n  const RegistrationScreen({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  State<RegistrationScreen> createState() => _RegistrationScreenState();\n}\n\nclass _RegistrationScreenState extends State<RegistrationScreen> {\n  final _email = TextEditingController();\n  final _phone = TextEditingController();\n  double _amount = 50000;\n  bool _terms = false;\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _email.dispose();\n    _phone.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  bool get _canContinue =>\n      _terms && _email.text.contains('@') && _phone.text.length >= 10;\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Register')),\n      body: Padding(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),\n        child: Column(\n          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n          children: [\n            TextField(\n              controller: _email,\n              keyboardType: TextInputType.emailAddress,\n              decoration: const InputDecoration(labelText: 'Email'),\n              onChanged: (_) => setState(() {}),\n            ),\n            const SizedBox(height: 12),\n            TextField(\n              controller: _phone,\n              keyboardType: TextInputType.phone,\n              decoration: const InputDecoration(labelText: 'Phone'),\n              onChanged: (_) => setState(() {}),\n            ),\n            const SizedBox(height: 24),\n            Text('Loan amount: ${_amount.round()}'),\n            Slider(\n              min: 10000,\n              max: 500000,\n              divisions: 49,\n              value: _amount,\n              label: _amount.round().toString(),\n              onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _amount = v),\n            ),\n            CheckboxListTile(\n              value: _terms,\n              title: const Text('I accept the terms and conditions'),\n              controlAffinity: ListTileControlAffinity.leading,\n              onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _terms = v ?? false),\n            ),\n            const Spacer(),\n            FilledButton(\n              onPressed: _canContinue\n                  ? () => Navigator.of(context).pushNamed('/offers')\n                  : null,\n              child: const Text('Continue'),\n            ),\n          ],\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n# kredito\n\nFlutter app (iOS + Android) for a consumer loan broker. The user registers\nwith an email and a phone number, picks the amount they want to borrow, accepts\nthe terms and gets a list of offers from partner banks. Two screens so far:\n`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`.\n\nAnalytics is PostHog (`posthog_flutter`), set up in `lib/analytics.dart` and\n`lib/main.dart`; screen views come from `PosthogObserver`. We are on the\nPostHog free tier. Product events are defined in `docs/EVENTS.md`; the\nscreens do not send any of them yet. Send events through `Analytics.capture`\nso the key and host stay in one place.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6ff9059-0b9a-4c59-ac96-8c6795444a07","uuid":"8ae99fba-5327-41e5-af97-b4b3f330d66c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:44:29.405Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\n/// Thin wrapper around PostHog so the key and host live in one place.\nclass Analytics {\n  static Future<void> init() async {\n    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n    await Posthog().setup(config);\n  }\n\n  /// Sends one event. [props] is optional.\n  static Future<void> capture(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass Offer {\n  const Offer(this.bank, this.months, this.rate);\n  final String bank;\n  final int months;\n  final double rate;\n}\